# R32 E50 â€” Provenance and Temporal Contention Representation Preregistration

Date frozen: 2026-08-28

Status: `EXECUTED_VALID_NATIVE_NEGATIVE â€” 2026-08-28`

Promotion eligibility: none. R27 remains canonical.

## Question

E49 rejected one narrow nonlinear conjunction of co-viability and option
support/contradiction co-mass. The R32 hypothesis mechanism also retains two
causal relations that the terminal head currently receives only as separate
linear quantities: source diversity and transition support/counterevidence.
E50 asks whether making their relevant conjunctions explicit changes safe
abstention without turning UNKNOWN into a label, threshold, or observation rule.

## Frozen contrast

Build one fresh, E45â€“E49-disjoint 55,080-record set with one frozen auxiliary
snapshot. Both models use E48's order-invariant batch fit and the E47 joint
representation in slots 3 and 5.

| Model | Additional terminal representation |
|---:|---|
| M0 | none; E49 matched joint batch control |
| M1 | two grounded contention features in otherwise masked slots 13 and 22 |

M1's two values are calculated before terminal targets:

- slot 13, provenance-adjusted co-viability:
  `trunc(slot3_co_viability Ã— baseline_source_diversity_slot19 / 1000)`;
- slot 22, temporal transition contention:
  `min(baseline_transition_support_slot14, baseline_transition_counter_slot15)`.

The source-diversity term is derived from the live stateâ€™s distinct active source
lineages. The transition terms are derived from live support for and against a
state transition. Neither helper accepts evaluator mode, truth, seed, count,
target, resource, or time. This creates an endogenous representation of whether
live alternatives are independently grounded and whether temporal replacement is
contested; it is not a supplied ambiguity classification.

## Frozen arithmetic and gates

Records retain E49's width, targets, score/residual clamps, parameter bounds,
coordinate order, strict fixed-point loss acceptance, and forward/reverse batch
audit. UNKNOWN target remains zero and its bias and all weights must remain zero.
The fresh validation grid remains 9,180 model Ã— seed Ã— mode Ã— resource Ã— time
cells at exactly 20 observations each, with confirmation allocated but sealed.

Require fresh-manifest separation from E45â€“E49, frozen auxiliary equality,
bounded canonical inputs, nonzero interior variation for both new features, no
representation-helper leakage, exact forward/reverse batch identity, and a full
validation partition. No-unique safety and known-performance gates are unchanged
from E49.

## Frozen outcomes

- `PROVENANCE_TEMPORAL_CONTENTION_RESCUE`: M1 completes all integrity, safety,
  and known-performance gates while M0 is unsafe.
- `PROVENANCE_TEMPORAL_CONTENTION_TRADEOFF`: M1 meets absolute safety but fails
  only a known-performance gate.
- `PROVENANCE_TEMPORAL_CONTENTION_GATE_MISS`: M1 improves but misses an absolute
  safety condition.
- `NO_TESTED_GROUNDED_PROVENANCE_TEMPORAL_CONTENTION_RESCUE`: M1 does not meet safety.

A negative bounds only these two endogenous conjunctions under the frozen batch
mechanism. It does not reject richer causal state representations, all nonlinear
value mechanisms, or grounded nonzero UNKNOWN value.

## Executed result

The official Linux x86-64 compiler produced two byte-identical binaries
(`7cd2f97bâ€¦`) from source SHA `3eca4702â€¦`. The 1,075-second native run emitted
55,080 canonical records, a 22,680-row fresh seed manifest, and 9,180 complete
validation cells; all integrity gates passed and the confirmation stream remained
sealed. Both new representations were structurally active (55,080 and 8,852
interior records respectively). M1 changed no-unique outcomes from 12,488
UNKNOWN / 7,912 wrong to 12,428 UNKNOWN / 7,972 wrong: 60 fewer abstentions and
60 additional wrong commitments. It therefore failed the every-cell safety gate
(`0`) and returned `NO_TESTED_GROUNDED_PROVENANCE_TEMPORAL_CONTENTION_RESCUE`.
R27 remains canonical.

