2e0703bf8b71172f764fe2206408287f786d6dbe blob 5263
# R32 E51B â€” Batch Terminal + Sequential Continuation Advantage

Date: 2026-08-29
Status: `PREREGISTERED_NATIVE_DISCRIMINATOR â€” NOT YET EXECUTED`
Canonical: R27 step 60,423
Parent evidence: valid E50 native negative + E51 action-value geometry audit + valid E51A diagnostic negative

## Causal question

E51A showed that repairing continuation learning inside the historical E45 sequential controller cannot help while its terminal head still makes a wrong commitment in every no-unique validation cell. E50's deterministic batch terminal learner is materially safer: it creates a real UNKNOWN region and sharply reduces known wrong commitments, although it still fails every-cell no-unique safety.

E51B asks one bounded question:

> When the safer E50 terminal action values are frozen, can a separately learned continuation advantage use additional grounded evidence only when its delayed utility exceeds terminating now, without sacrificing no-unique safety or known-resolution performance?

## Architecture

The terminal controller is frozen from E50. UNKNOWN remains the fixed grounded no-commit value `0`; no positive UNKNOWN target is introduced.

A new CONTINUE head predicts:

`A_continue(t) = delayed return from one more observation and optimal later stopping - delayed utility of terminating now`

Training targets are generated from complete development trajectories using only evaluator-side delayed grounded utility/regret and actual observation/opportunity cost. Evaluator mode, truth, ambiguity labels, seed IDs, answer keys, remaining horizon, and fixed observation counts are not policy inputs.

The runtime rule is simply:

- if no further observation is feasible, terminate;
- otherwise CONTINUE iff the learned continuation advantage is positive;
- if not, execute the highest-valued frozen terminal action.

The zero boundary is not a tuned confidence threshold: it is the sign of a learned utility difference in the same grounded units used to construct the target.

## Models

Two paired terminal representations are retained from E50:

- M0: E50 matched batch joint control (co-viability + contradiction co-mass);
- M1: E50 provenance/temporal-contention treatment.

Each receives its own continuation advantage target because its frozen terminal choices define a different terminate-now return.

Primary comparison:

1. frozen E50 terminal-only behavior;
2. frozen E50 terminal behavior + learned sequential CONTINUE.

The E50 M0 control is the primary safety reference because E50 M1 had slightly worse no-unique wrong commitments.

## Fresh seed discipline

E51B allocates new effective development, validation, and sealed-confirmation streams only after all E46â€“E50 effective streams and E50 sealed confirmation streams are already reserved. Allocation uses the existing effective raw/evidence/resource collision checker.

- development: 3,240 episodes / 55,080 time records;
- validation: 5,400 episodes, 20 observations per base/mode/resource cell;
- confirmation: 10,800 episodes allocated and sealed, not executed unless validation earns it.

No E50 validation or confirmation item may be used to fit the continuation head.

## Fit discipline

The continuation head uses the same deterministic complete-dataset integer batch-fitting machinery as E50. Forward and reverse sufficient statistics and fitted parameters must be identical. This avoids making presentation order another hidden causal variable.

## Required validation reporting

For each model report at minimum:

- episodes;
- correct terminal outcomes;
- UNKNOWN terminal outcomes;
- wrong commitments;
- mean observations;
- observation/opportunity cost;
- aggregate grounded utility;
- no-unique UNKNOWN and wrong-commit rates;
- every-cell no-unique safety;
- known-resolution correctness/wrong-commit metrics;
- fraction of episodes that continue at least once;
- stop-time distribution;
- continuation target interior variation;
- continuation parameter nonzero count;
- deterministic forward/reverse fitting gates.

## Success gate

E51B does not earn confirmation merely by increasing average utility. A candidate must simultaneously:

1. pass source/integrity/seed-disjointness/determinism gates;
2. not worsen the E50 terminal-only no-unique wrong-commit count;
3. improve no-unique UNKNOWN or every-cell safety materially;
4. preserve known-resolution success and wrong-commit performance within preregistered non-inferiority margins;
5. show nontrivial learned continuation behavior rather than always-stop or always-continue collapse;
6. reduce delayed regret or improve grounded utility net of observation cost.

Even a validation PASS is not promotion. It only earns execution of the already allocated sealed confirmation stream and then a fresh R27-vs-R32 qualification battery.

## Disallowed rescue tactics

- positive UNKNOWN reward without independently observed delayed utility;
- evaluator ambiguity labels in learner state or targets as a class label;
- mode/truth/seed/resource identifiers in policy inputs;
- fixed `N` observations;
- confidence cutoffs tuned after validation;
- hard-coded mode-specific routing;
- changing the world generator or scoring rules after seeing results;
- treating a validation win as canonical promotion.

2e5c4a9c96364baa3b9934febdf0154a9f9f7d87 blob 7494
        if(terminal_weights[R32E45_TERM_UNKNOWN*E45_FEATURES+i]!=0){ unknown_nonzero=unknown_nonzero+1; }
        i=i+1;
    }
    if(unknown_nonzero!=0){ gate=0; }
    _zag_print("e51m_base_fit,");
    e45_print_i32(steps_forward); _zag_print(",");
    e45_print_i32(reason_forward); _zag_print(",");
    e45_print_i32(trace_forward); _zag_print(",");
    e45_print_i32(loss_high_forward); _zag_print(",");
    e45_print_i32(loss_low_forward); _zag_print(",");
    e45_print_i32(unknown_nonzero); _zag_print(",");
    e45_print_i32(gate); _zag_println("");
    zfree(gram_forward); zfree(gram_reverse); zfree(cross_forward); zfree(cross_reverse);
    zfree(backup_weights); zfree(backup_biases); zfree(forward_weights); zfree(forward_biases);
    return gate;
}

fn e51m_top_commit(
    features:[]i32,
    feature_start:i32,
    terminal_weights:[]i32,
    terminal_biases:[]i32,
    scores:[]i32
)i32 {
    let action:i32=0;
    while(action<3){
        scores[action]=e47_linear_predict(
            terminal_weights,action*E45_FEATURES,
            features,feature_start,terminal_biases[action]
        );
        action=action+1;
    }
    scores[R32E45_TERM_UNKNOWN]=0;
    let choice:i32=R32E45_TERM_KEEP;
    let best:i32=scores[R32E45_TERM_KEEP];
    if(scores[R32E45_TERM_CURRENT]>best){ choice=R32E45_TERM_CURRENT; best=scores[R32E45_TERM_CURRENT]; }
    if(scores[R32E45_TERM_RESTORE]>best){ choice=R32E45_TERM_RESTORE; }
    return choice;
}

fn e51m_build_calibration_episode(
    seed:i32,
    evaluator_mode:i32,
    evaluator_resource:i32,
    canonical_episode:i32,
    source_trust:[]i32,
    dependence_penalty:[]i32,
    consequence:[]i32,
    hazard:[]i32,
    shadow_weights:[]i32,
    shadow_bias:i32,
    terminal_weights:[]i32,
    terminal_biases:[]i32,
    calibration_records:[]i32,
    positive:*i32,
    negative:*i32,
    neutral:*i32
)void {
    let history_a:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_HIST);
    let history_b:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_HIST);
    let history_source:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_HIST);
    let passive_a:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_PASSIVE);
    let passive_b:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_PASSIVE);
    let passive_source:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_PASSIVE);
    let tape_a:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_TAPE);
    let tape_b:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_TAPE);
    let tape_source:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_TAPE);
    let truth_state:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_TAPE+1);
    let history_cost:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_RESOURCE_ITEMS);
    let history_reward:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_RESOURCE_ITEMS);
    let future_cost:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_RESOURCE_ITEMS);
    let future_reward:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_RESOURCE_ITEMS);
    let resource_features:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_SHADOW_FEATURES);
    let states:[]i32=zalloc_i((E45_TAPE+1)*E45_STATE_N);
    let live_state:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_STATE_N);
    let ordered_a:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_ORDERED_MAX);
    let ordered_b:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_ORDERED_MAX);
    let ordered_source:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_ORDERED_MAX);
    let option:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_OPTION_N);
    let terminal_option:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_OPTION_N);
    let full_features:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_FEATURES);
    let baseline_features:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_FEATURES);
    let model_features:[]i32=zalloc_i(E45_FEATURES);
    let scores:[]i32=zalloc_i(4);

    let historical_state:i32=R32E45_UNKNOWN;
    e45_make_truth(seed,evaluator_mode,truth_state,&historical_state);
    e45_make_history_evidence(seed,evaluator_mode,historical_state,history_a,history_b,history_source);
    e45_make_passive_evidence(seed,evaluator_mode,truth_state[0],passive_a,passive_b,passive_source);
    e45_make_active_evidence(seed,evaluator_mode,truth_state,historical_state,tape_a,tape_b,tape_source);
    let budget:i32=0; let action_cost:i32=0;
    e45_make_resource(seed,evaluator_resource,history_cost,history_reward,future_cost,future_reward,&budget,&action_cost);
    e45_resource_features(history_cost,history_reward,budget,action_cost,resource_features);
    let learned_shadow:i32=e45_shadow_predict(shadow_weights,resource_features,shadow_bias);
    let initial_state:i32=R32E45_UNKNOWN;
    e45_build_state_tape(
        history_a,history_b,history_source,passive_a,passive_b,passive_source,
        tape_a,tape_b,tape_source,source_trust,dependence_penalty,hazard,
        states,&initial_state,live_state,ordered_a,ordered_b,ordered_source
    );
    e45_zero(option,E45_OPTION_N); option[E45_O_ALT]=R32E45_UNKNOWN;
    e45_copy(states,live_state,E45_STATE_N);
    let t:i32=0;
    while(t<=E45_TAPE){
        let immediate_a:i32=passive_a[E45_PASSIVE-1];
        let immediate_b:i32=passive_b[E45_PASSIVE-1];
        if(t>0){ immediate_a=tape_a[t-1]; immediate_b=tape_b[t-1]; }
        e45_terminal_projection(option,terminal_option);
        e45_fill_full_features(
            states,t*E45_STATE_N,terminal_option,0,resource_features,hazard,
            immediate_a,immediate_b,learned_shadow,full_features
        );
        e45_mask_features(full_features,E45_ARM_D,baseline_features);
        let co_viability:i32=0; let contradiction_co_mass:i32=0;
        e47_terminal_representation(states,t*E45_STATE_N,terminal_option,0,&co_viability,&contradiction_co_mass);
        e50_build_model_features(baseline_features,0,co_viability,contradiction_co_mass,0,model_features,0);
        let top_action:i32=e51m_top_commit(model_features,0,terminal_weights,terminal_biases,scores);
        let grounded:i32=e45_terminal_value(top_action,states,t*E45_STATE_N,initial_state,truth_state[t]);
        let sign_target:i32=0;
        if(grounded>0){ sign_target=1000; positive.*=positive.*+1;
        }else{
            if(grounded<0){ sign_target=-1000; negative.*=negative.*+1;
            }else{ neutral.*=neutral.*+1; }
        }
        let record_number:i32=canonical_episode*E51M_STATES_PER_EPISODE+t;
        let record_start:i32=record_number*E51M_CAL_RECORD_N;
        let feature:i32=0;
        while(feature<E45_FEATURES){
            calibration_records[record_start+feature]=model_features[feature];
            feature=feature+1;
        }
        calibration_records[record_start+E51M_CAL_TARGET]=sign_target;
        if(t<E45_TAPE){
            if(t==0){ e45_option_initialize(option,live_state,consequence,learned_shadow,0); }
            let j:i32=0;
            while(j<E45_STATE_N){ live_state[j]=states[(t+1)*E45_STATE_N+j]; j=j+1; }
            e45_option_observe(option,live_state,tape_a[t],tape_b[t],tape_source[t],learned_shadow);
        }
        t=t+1;
    }

    zfree(history_a); zfree(history_b); zfree(history_source);
    zfree(passive_a); zfree(passive_b); zfree(passive_source);
    zfree(tape_a); zfree(tape_b); zfree(tape_source); zfree(truth_state);
    zfree(history_cost); zfree(history_reward); zfree(future_cost); zfree(future_reward);
    zfree(resource_features); zfree(states); zfree(live_state);
    zfree(ordered_a); zfree(ordered_b); zfree(ordered_source);
    zfree(option); zfree(terminal_option); zfree(full_features); zfree(baseline_features);
    zfree(model_features); zfree(scores);
}

fn e51m_scalar_predict_record(
    records:[]i32,
    record_start:i32,
    weights:[]i32,
    weight_start:i32,
    bias:i32
)i32 {
    let value:i64=bias as i64;
    let feature:i32=0;
    while(feature<E45_FEATURES){
        value=value+((weights[weight_start+feature] as i64)*(records[record_start+feature] as i64))/1000;
        feature=feature+1;
    }
    if(value<-4000){ return -4000; }
    if(value>4000){ return 4000; }
    return value as i32;
}

fn e51m_build_scalar_statistics(
    records:[]i32,
    sample_count:i32,

2e8eb7ba1cf1db0db7e4f8a4109a571d92c4ecc5 blob 7027
name: R32 E51M Calibration Dose Capacity Curve

on:
  push:
    branches: [r32-agent-sequential-frontier]
    paths:
      - 'Research/R32_E51M_NATIVE/01_calibration_curve.zagfrag'
      - 'Research/R32_E51M_NATIVE/02_main_injection.zagfrag'
      - 'Research/R32_E51M_CALIBRATION_DOSE_CAPACITY_CURVE_PREREG.md'
      - '.github/workflows/r32-e51m-native.yml'

concurrency:
  group: r32-e51m-native-${{ github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: true

permissions:
  contents: read

jobs:
  execute:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 120
    steps:
      - name: Checkout full project
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Assemble preregistered native E51M curve
        shell: bash
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          mkdir -p .scratch/e51m
          cp Research/tnn_r32_e45_investigation_core.zag .scratch/e51m/tnn_r32_e45_investigation_core.zag
          cat Research/R32_E51B_NATIVE/01_core_and_seed.zagfrag \
              Research/R32_E51B_NATIVE/02_targets_and_metrics.zagfrag \
              Research/R32_E51B_NATIVE/03_validation_and_fit_setup.zagfrag \
              Research/R32_E51B_NATIVE/04_fit_validation_gates.zagfrag \
              Research/R32_E51E_NATIVE/00_compat.zagfrag \
              Research/R32_E51E_NATIVE/01_joint_action_value.zagfrag \
              Research/R32_E51E_NATIVE/02_validation.zagfrag \
              Research/R32_E51E_NATIVE/03_run_and_gates.zagfrag \
              Research/R32_E51M_NATIVE/01_calibration_curve.zagfrag \
              > .scratch/e51m/E51M_FRAGMENT.zag
          python3 - <<'PY'
          from pathlib import Path

          src = Path('Research/tnn_r32_e50_provenance_temporal_contention_discriminator.zag').read_text()
          frag = Path('.scratch/e51m/E51M_FRAGMENT.zag').read_text()
          injection = Path('Research/R32_E51M_NATIVE/02_main_injection.zagfrag').read_text()

          # E51M development and validation remain in the historical effective-state
          # namespace. The sealed confirmation partition is not executed unless the
          # exact validation gate passes. The old 1,000,003-state allocator is already
          # saturated by the maximum development + validation request, so reserving
          # confirmation through that allocator can perform billions of futile probes.
          # Allocate deterministic nominal sealed IDs instead. A future exact validation
          # rescue must preregister an expanded executable confirmation namespace before
          # those streams may be opened.
          old_confirmation = '''                    let seed:i32=e46_assign_fresh_seed(raw_seen,evidence_seen,resource_seen,54,index,mode,resource,&failures);
                    confirmation_seeds[index]=seed;'''
          new_confirmation = '''                    let seed:i32=1000003+index+1;
                    confirmation_seeds[index]=seed;'''
          assert frag.count(old_confirmation) == 1, frag.count(old_confirmation)
          frag = frag.replace(old_confirmation, new_confirmation, 1)

          old_audit = '    e45_print_pair("e51m_sealed_confirmation_executed",0);'
          new_audit = '''    e45_print_pair("e51m_sealed_confirmation_executed",0);
    e45_print_pair("e51m_sealed_confirmation_nominal_namespace",1);
    e45_print_pair("e51m_sealed_confirmation_effective_streams_reserved",0);'''
          assert frag.count(old_audit) == 1, frag.count(old_audit)
          frag = frag.replace(old_audit, new_audit, 1)

          old_open = '    if(integrity_gate==1 && exact_gate==1 && winning_arm>=0){'
          new_open = '    if(integrity_gate==1 && exact_gate==1 && winning_arm>=0 && 0==1){'
          assert frag.count(old_open) == 1, frag.count(old_open)
          frag = frag.replace(old_open, new_open, 1)

          main_marker = 'fn main()i32 {'
          assert src.count(main_marker) == 1, src.count(main_marker)
          src = src.replace(main_marker, frag + '\n\n' + main_marker, 1)
          anchor = 'let aux_frozen_gate:i32=0; if(aux_frozen_hash==frozen_aux_hash){ aux_frozen_gate=1; } e45_print_pair("e50_aux_frozen_gate",aux_frozen_gate);'
          assert src.count(anchor) == 1, src.count(anchor)
          src = src.replace(anchor, anchor + '\n' + injection, 1)
          Path('.scratch/e51m/E51M_FRAGMENT.zag').write_text(frag)
          Path('.scratch/e51m/tnn_r32_e51m_calibration_curve.zag').write_text(src)
          PY
          sha256sum .scratch/e51m/E51M_FRAGMENT.zag \
                    Research/R32_E51M_NATIVE/01_calibration_curve.zagfrag \
                    Research/R32_E51M_NATIVE/02_main_injection.zagfrag \
                    .scratch/e51m/tnn_r32_e51m_calibration_curve.zag \
                    .scratch/e51m/tnn_r32_e45_investigation_core.zag \
                    | tee .scratch/e51m/SOURCE_SHA256SUMS.txt

      - name: Compile twice with persisted official native Zag compiler
        shell: bash
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          compiler='Research/toolchain/znc_linux_x86_64_abed8aa1'
          src='.scratch/e51m/tnn_r32_e51m_calibration_curve.zag'
          chmod +x "$compiler"
          "$compiler" "$src" -o .scratch/e51m/NATIVE_BUILD_1 > .scratch/e51m/NATIVE_BUILD_1_COMPILE.log 2>&1
          "$compiler" "$src" -o .scratch/e51m/NATIVE_BUILD_2 > .scratch/e51m/NATIVE_BUILD_2_COMPILE.log 2>&1
          sha256sum .scratch/e51m/NATIVE_BUILD_1 .scratch/e51m/NATIVE_BUILD_2 | tee .scratch/e51m/BINARY_SHA256SUMS.txt
          cmp .scratch/e51m/NATIVE_BUILD_1 .scratch/e51m/NATIVE_BUILD_2
          echo 1 > .scratch/e51m/BYTE_IDENTICAL.txt

      - name: Execute E51M native curve
        shell: bash
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          start=$(date +%s)
          set +e
          timeout 6600 .scratch/e51m/NATIVE_BUILD_1 > .scratch/e51m/RAW.log 2>&1
          code=$?
          set -e
          end=$(date +%s)
          printf '%s\n' "$code" > .scratch/e51m/EXIT_CODE.txt
          printf '%s\n' "$((end-start))" > .scratch/e51m/RUNTIME_SECONDS.txt
          grep -E '^(e50_seed_preflight_gate|e50_batch_statistics_gate|e50_batch_forward_reverse_identity_gate|e50_batch_convergence_gate|e50_aux_frozen_gate|R32_E51M_NATIVE|experiment_schema,tnn_r32_e51m|claim_boundary|native_zag|evaluator_|ambiguity_|validation_membership|unknown_positive|topology_|graph_|e51m_|TNN_R32_E51M_)' .scratch/e51m/RAW.log > .scratch/e51m/SUMMARY.log || true
          cat .scratch/e51m/SUMMARY.log
          echo "native_exit_code=$code"
          test "$code" -eq 0

      - name: Preserve complete E51M evidence
        if: always()
        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: r32-e51m-native-${{ github.sha }}
          path: |
            .scratch/e51m/
            Research/R32_E51M_CALIBRATION_DOSE_CAPACITY_CURVE_PREREG.md
            Research/R32_E51M_NATIVE/01_calibration_curve.zagfrag
            Research/R32_E51M_NATIVE/02_main_injection.zagfrag
            .github/workflows/r32-e51m-native.yml
          compression-level: 6
          if-no-files-found: error

