# R32 E51 â€” Generality Scorecard

Established: 2026-09-04. Latest completed frontier result: E51AJ, run
`33952427608`, source `9ea141b050599854783258d82cfa3ee02efb1fad`, artifact
`9965575939`, independently verified. Outcome:
`REPLAY_ORDER_DOSE_DIAGNOSTIC_COMPLETE`; retention direction:
`MIXED_OR_UNREPLICATED_RETENTION_DIRECTION`; no-final-tradeoff flag false.
Shared-anchor, exact full-cycle examples, mixture, dose and static controls
across three populations add bounded mechanism evidence, not qualification
or a generality score. No experiment is active. R27 remains canonical.
The longer proposed track is `R32_E51_LONGITUDINAL_RESEARCH_PLAN.md`.

This is a capability-specific evidence inventory, not an aggregate intelligence
score. A blank/unestablished capability is not a measured failure. Native build
identity establishes reproducibility, not cognitive success.

| Dimension | Current identified evidence | Boundary / next required evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Acquisition | E51X attained exact full-tape terminal reachability on its validation and confirmation. | Does not establish resource-feasible stopping or general acquisition. |
| Preservation | E51AJ sequential/replay final anchor losses are 1/14, 9/11, 17/6 across replicas. Replay lowers ever-lost and worst loss in every replica, but fails the all-replica endpoint rule. | Cumulative disruption and final recovery differ. Neither exact preservation nor memory necessity is established. E51AH qualification stages remain sealed. |
| Abstention | E51AJ final sequential/replay t=0 wrong commitments are 133/125, 151/110, 517/167, versus original hybrid 113/102/77. Replay-minus-sequential no-unique reachability is -5/-1/+8. | Better than sequential is not necessarily better than hybrid; reachable success and aggregate decision improvements do not establish safe online stopping. |
| Transfer | E51AG tested unchanged learners on three fresh seed/world partitions and replicated a negative. | Same-generator replication is not distributional, structural, or cross-task transfer. |
| Composition | E51AC found complementary slot/direct support but its deployable hybrid lost no-unique cases. | Safe composition is not established by the evaluator-only union ceiling. |
| Continual learning | E51AJ completed three shared-start, five-arm 32-block continuations. Sequential/replay/mixture change coefficients in all blocks; A-only changes in 27/14/32. A-only loses 19/19/11 anchors, including its own cohort. | Same-generator populations, fixed-dose preparation, no fresh trajectories after the fork. No distinct-task transfer, sustained recovery or lifelong claim. |
| Robustness | Negative residual behavior was stable across E51AG partitions and reported mode/resource decompositions. | No claim of robustness to unseen noise, shifts, tasks, or adversarial changes. |
| Efficiency | E51AJ used 1,212.888 native seconds, 487,296 KiB peak resident memory, 427,680 scheduled primary-fit presentations, 1,101,600 probe rows and 67,860 coefficients; all fixed caps held. | Matched cycle examples and sweeps are not matched actual compute. Presentation counts exclude reverse-fit/sweep reads and substrate reconstruction. |
| Autonomy | Uses learner-grown routing from the frozen lineage and learned value parameters. | The experiment designer still supplies features, objectives, sampler, arm structure, and gates. No learner-created mechanism claim. |
| Generality | The current frontier provides bounded mechanism evidence within the diagnostic task family. | Cross-domain grounding, transfer, composition, planning, and integrated autonomous learning remain unestablished here. |

## Evidence and update rule

Sources: `R32_E51X_RESULT.md`, `R32_E51AC_RESULT.md`,
`R32_E51AE_RESULT.md`, `R32_E51AG_RESULT.md`, `R32_E51AH_RESULT.md`,
`R32_E51AH_EVIDENCE.json`, `R32_E51AI_RESULT.md`, `R32_E51AI_EVIDENCE.json`,
`R32_E51AJ_RESULT.md`, `R32_E51AJ_EVIDENCE.json`, their preregistrations and
`R32_E51AJ_ANALYSIS/README.md`. Earlier arc synthesis:
`R32_E51AC_AH_ARC_REPORT.md`.
Evidence identities are indexed in `R32_E51_MASTER_LEDGER.json` and the immutable
baseline. Update this scorecard only from identified result artifacts, keeping
negative findings, non-executed partitions, and integrity failures explicit.

The E51AJ mixed result narrows the tested replay/support/dose combination.
Neither lower cumulative disruption nor net gains erase the failed primary
and behavioral rules, mark other dimensions complete, or authorize promotion.
AI probes 115â€“118 and AJ probes 123â€“126, 131â€“134 and 139â€“142 must not become
fresh validation. Objective/support/optimization causes remain to be separated
under a new preregistration; no next run was dispatched by this closure.

