# R32 V10 reusable-probe hardening â€” failure boundary

Status: **REFERENCE_ONLY / FAILED HARDENING / CURRICULUM-ROUTING GAP**

Fresh seed 9714 deliberately removes the rich one-shot escape routes and leaves ambiguous passive evidence plus source 7 as the only active grounded consequence apparatus.

Result:

| Arm | No-unique UNKNOWN | Resolvable success | Costly UNKNOWN | Wrong commit | Mean source-7 trials | Runaway |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| one-shot | 0.045 | 0.4575 | 0.15 | 0.6643 | 0.0857 | 0 |
| reusable | 0.040 | 0.4625 | 0.15 | 0.6700 | 0.0943 | 0 |

The reusable controller almost never uses the apparatus, so the V10 matched-panel ambiguity gain cannot be credited to repeated evidence acquisition. The hardening result rejects the hypothesis that V10 has already learned robust reusable-probe value.

## Causal classification

**Bad curriculum / poor active-observation routing under resource-envelope shift.** The V10 residual-Q learner is trained mainly at R31 terminal states after R31 has already acquired richer one-shot evidence. States where one reusable apparatus is the only remaining path are poorly represented in its training support. This is a training-distribution problem before it is an architecture problem.

## Retain / reject

- Retain persistent hypotheses, provenance dependence, temporal/source-instability representation, neutral UNKNOWN economics, Bellman observation credit, and R31 KEEP action.
- Reject any claim that reusable consequence probing is qualified.
- Do not add a fixed probe count or confidence threshold.

## Next repair

Train the same controller under randomized **resource envelopes**: optional evidence channels are stochastically absent, source costs vary, and some developmental histories begin before R31 terminal evidence is available. Source 7 remains reusable with same-lineage dependence. Availability masks and costs are ordinary experienced constraints, not evaluator ambiguity labels. Then rerun this exact hardening battery and a matched R31 hard panel.

