# R32 E45â€“E48 Native Terminal-Controller Report

Date: 2026-08-28

Status: `FOUR VALID NATIVE NEGATIVES â€” R27 REMAINS CANONICAL`

## Result

The official persisted Linux x86-64 Zag compiler now provides native authority
for the repaired E45 terminal-controller battery and its three bounded follow-up
discriminators. This resolves the materialization issue for these experiments; it
does not qualify R32. Every experiment below is a valid negative under its frozen
question, so R27 remains the canonical TNN.

| Experiment | Isolated question | Native result | Bounded conclusion |
|---|---|---|---|
| E45 | Does the repaired causal evaluator permit safe terminal control? | No: every no-unique D episode made a wrong commit. | This is a real terminal-controller failure, not evaluator collapse. |
| E46 | Can presentation order alone repair it? | No: schedules created a large abstention/resolution tradeoff, but none passed all gates. | No tested order rescue. |
| E47 | Do two grounded continuous co-presence features repair the blocked online linear head? | No: both features varied, while every joint-model no-unique decision still committed wrongly. | No tested representation rescue under blocked online linear fitting. |
| E48 | Does a specified order-invariant batch fit, with or without E47's joint representation, repair it? | No: batch fit improved abstention but neither arm was safe in every no-unique cell. | No tested batch safety rescue under the current linear value geometry. |

## Native evidence

E45 was frozen at source SHA256
`b404223658f51dc95cc20a76af515e8a3bc828a373e3a244d12a2cd7fb3d9f1e`.
E46 and E47 are preserved native negatives at source SHA256
`6e78954f00b107829ee50f988704d6a79a6ac924f4e38679acd293018edec51e` and
`b7b49f4d23e67c4370d6ac449622ac828687cf67df9b5404f2120edff73becbd`.

E48 is the latest authoritative ledger. Its source SHA256 is
`24e8098f805fa1f1548250ac5c7968658caeb8293534b2cb5f2ae0d06d442d0a`.
Two official x86-64 builds were byte-identical at SHA256
`5efdab6533f66fabe9ef90c9edd6092e8c90cceeef58c8fe44e1fd4dc680a884`.
The complete 1,065-second raw ledger SHA256 is
`0df6a38241c63275f0fd2eea15154875dadbce46580921811ba7fcec00f5d950`.
It includes every canonical training record, final terminal parameter, batch
audit, and fresh validation row. Its stored checksum manifest validates all
preserved files.

## E48 detail

All four models used the same 55,080 canonical records, the same frozen
auxiliary snapshot, target semantics, evaluator, and fresh validation grid.
M0/M1 used the frozen blocked one-pass update; M2/M3 used complete-dataset
integer normal-equation coordinate sweeps, retaining only strict reductions in
the exact fixed-point clipped loss. Forward and reverse record traversal were
identical in statistics, parameters, accepted sweep counts, stopping points, and
loss traces.

| Model | No-unique UNKNOWN | No-unique wrong | Safe cells | Known success | Known wrong |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| M0 online baseline | 0 | 20,400 | 0 / 1,020 | 54,182 | 17,218 |
| M1 online joint | 0 | 20,400 | 0 / 1,020 | 54,182 | 17,218 |
| M2 batch baseline | 12,219 | 8,181 | 346 / 1,020 | 50,338 | 2,158 |
| M3 batch joint | 12,260 | 8,140 | 318 / 1,020 | 48,575 | 1,632 |

The UNKNOWN target was zero on every canonical record. Its bias and all
UNKNOWN-head weights remained exactly zero. Thus UNKNOWN continued to mean that
no commit action had positive grounded value; no ambiguity category, confidence
threshold, or fixed observation count was introduced.

## What is and is not established

E45â€“E48 establish a failure of these frozen terminal-controller combinations.
They do not reject the R32 architecture, grounded UNKNOWN, endogenous richer
causal representation, or a small nonlinear grounded commit-value mechanism.
The next experiment must preserve the evaluator, target semantics, fresh seed
separation, full-cell safety gate, and known-performance gate while changing one
such mechanism only.

## Authoritative files

- `R32_E45_NEGATIVE_RESULTS_AND_EVALUATOR_REPAIR.md`
- `R32_E48_ONLINE_BATCH_REPRESENTATION_PREREGISTRATION.md`
- `R32_E48_ONLINE_BATCH_REPRESENTATION_NEGATIVE_24E8098F_NO_TESTED_BATCH_SAFETY_RESCUE_EVIDENCE.json`
